@FX BALL_ORACLE|THE CRYSTAL BALL|solo|chart_nines
@GAP nothing at all|the symbol beside the number they ended on|Every 2-digit start minus its digit sum is a multiple of 9; the device re-deals the chart each play so all of those cells share one random symbol no other cell shows.
@P gaze
@S The mantis stills. Something is already written.
@W 900
@S Think of any two-digit number.
@B press when you have it
@P think
@S Add its two digits together.
@B press when done
@S Take that away from your number.
@B press when you have it
@S Now find your answer on my chart.
@W 700
@M press once you know your symbol
@P raise
@S Picture it. Burn it into your mind.
@W 900
@S It does not need to see. It only waits.
@W 800
@P reveal
@R {SYMBOL}
@W 700
@S The mantis was never guessing.
@E
@FX BOOK_ORACLE|THE MANTIS BOOK|solo|book_1089
@GAP nothing at all|the word their number led them to|Every legal start reaches 1089, digit sum 18; the page is picked at random each play, so the word changes every time.
@P gaze
@S The mantis stills. Something is already written.
@W 900
@S Think of a three-digit number.
@W 600
@S First digit two or more bigger than the last.
@B press when you have it
@P think
@S Reverse it. Take the smaller from the larger.
@B press when done
@S Reverse THAT answer. Add the two together.
@B press when done
@S Add up the digits of your total.
@B press when you have it
@S Count that many words into my page.
@W 700
@Q press once you have your word|18|On a quiet night the old mantis climbed the garden wall and watched as a huge yellow moon rose over the pond.~Deep in the jungle a green mantis waited on a leaf while rain drummed softly on a umbrella made of giant leaves.~Every single morning the young mantis practiced her dance until the busy ants stopped to watch the lantern glow at dawn.~High above the quiet meadow the wind carried seeds past a sleepy mantis who dreamed of a castle made of honey.~When the circus came to town the mantis sold tickets and every child begged to ride the dragon on the painted carousel.
@P raise
@S Your number chose that word. Not me.
@W 900
@P reveal
@R {WORD}
@W 700
@S The mantis was never guessing.
@E
